Skip the Numba/CFFI complex kernel tests from cffi 1.17.

Numba cannot type CFFI complex arguments: see map_type in
numba/core/typing/cffi_utils.py. From cffi 1.17 the complex ctypes are named
_cffi_{float,double}_complex_t, which that mapping does not know, so the test
errors rather than failing cleanly.

Backport of the upstream condition from DOLFINx commit aa9570ddf8
(FEniCS/dolfinx#4397), which replaced the narrower 1.17/2.0.0 range with an
open-ended one. Module-level 'cffi = pytest.importorskip("cffi")' already
binds the name in every release patched here.

0.8 has no marks on the parameters at all.

--- a/python/test/unit/fem/test_custom_assembler.py
+++ b/python/test/unit/fem/test_custom_assembler.py
@@ -224,7 +224,35 @@
     sink(A_local, dofmap)
 
 
-@pytest.mark.parametrize("dtype", [np.float32, np.float64, np.complex64, np.complex128])
+@pytest.mark.parametrize(
+    "dtype",
+    [
+        np.float32,
+        np.float64,
+        pytest.param(
+            np.complex64,
+            marks=[
+                pytest.mark.skipif(
+                    cffi.__version_info__ >= (1, 17),
+                    reason="Numba cannot type CFFI complex arguments, see map_type in "
+                    "numba/core/typing/cffi_utils.py. From cffi 1.17 the complex ctypes "
+                    "are named _cffi_{float,double}_complex_t.",
+                ),
+            ],
+        ),
+        pytest.param(
+            np.complex128,
+            marks=[
+                pytest.mark.skipif(
+                    cffi.__version_info__ >= (1, 17),
+                    reason="Numba cannot type CFFI complex arguments, see map_type in "
+                    "numba/core/typing/cffi_utils.py. From cffi 1.17 the complex ctypes "
+                    "are named _cffi_{float,double}_complex_t.",
+                ),
+            ],
+        ),
+    ],
+)
